---
import data from '../../data/app-assessments.json';
import commercial from '../../data/app-commercial-facts.json';
import rubric from '../../data/app-design-rubric.json';
import {screensFor,screenFor,dateLabel} from '../../lib/app-library';
import ProfileSelector from './ProfileSelector.astro';
const {app}=Astro.props;const a=data.apps.find(x=>x.app_id===app.id);const shots=screensFor(app.id);const cost=commercial.apps.find(x=>x.app_id===app.id);
const names:Record<string,string>={concern_evidenced:'Concern evidenced',ethical_baseline_observed:'Ethical baseline observed',redemptive_candidate:'Redemptive candidate',redemptive_practice_evidenced:'Redemptive practice evidenced',mixed:'Mixed findings',not_assessed:'Flow review needed',not_applicable:'Not applicable'};
const findings=a?Object.entries(a.dimensions).filter(([,d])=>!['not_assessed','not_applicable'].includes(d.status)):[];
const principleFor=(id:string)=>rubric.principles.find(p=>p.id===id);
const evidenceScreen=(url:string)=>screenFor(url.split('/').filter(Boolean).at(-1));
const places=[['word','The Word'],['person','The person'],['practice','The practice'],['people','The people'],['makers','The makers']];
const attention=shots.filter(s=>/reminder|streak|progress|routine|notification/i.test(s.screen_name+' '+s.caption));
const coverage=(id:string)=>{const d=a?.dimensions[id];if(d)return names[d.status];if(id==='money_access')return cost?.access_scopes.length?'Free / paid scope documented':cost?.iap.products.length?'Store prices documented':'Access evidence incomplete';if(a?.dimension_reviews?.[id])return 'Reviewed; checks remaining';if(id==='attention_agency')return attention.length?'Candidate mechanics; controls unchecked':'Controls not captured';return 'No scoped finding yet';};
---
<section class="lib-section lib-design-profile" id="assessment" aria-labelledby="design-findings-title">
 <header class="lib-design-heading"><h2 id="design-findings-title">Design nutrition</h2><p>What is in the app, how it serves people, and what the evidence can tell us.</p></header>
 <div data-profile-selector="Design assessment">
 <nav class="lib-nutrition-grid" data-selector-list aria-label="Explore an assessment dimension">{rubric.dimensions.map(d=><a id={'nutrition-tab-'+d.id} href={'#dimension-'+d.id}><strong>{d.label}</strong><span>{coverage(d.id)}</span></a>)}</nav>
 {rubric.dimensions.map(d=>{const finding=a?.dimensions[d.id];const review=a?.dimension_reviews?.[d.id];const evidence=finding?.evidence.map(e=>evidenceScreen(e.url)).filter(Boolean)||[];return <section class="lib-nutrition-panel" id={'dimension-'+d.id}>
  <header><h3>{d.label}</h3><p class="lib-note">{d.principle_ids.map((id,n)=>{const p=principleFor(id);return <Fragment>{n>0?' · ':''}<a href={p?.url}>{p?.name}</a></Fragment>;})}</p></header>
  {d.id==='money_access'?<div class="lib-money-summary"><div><h4>Access and paywalls</h4>{cost?.access_scopes.length?cost.access_scopes.map(s=><p>{s.summary} <a href={s.source_url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Publisher source</a></p>):<p>The sources reviewed do not establish the free/paid capability boundary.</p>}{app.id==='app.hallow.Hallow'&&<p>The publisher describes a dismissible subscription screen and premium-content markers. These are documented instructions, rather than a captured test of the flow.</p>}<p class="lib-note">Purchase flow still needs checking: paywall dismissal, default plan, trial renewal disclosure, restore and cancellation. A listed price alone does not establish informed consent or an easy exit.</p><a href="#cost-access">All access, billing and publisher sources</a></div><div><h4>Listed in-app prices</h4>{cost?.iap.products.length?<><ul class="lib-price-list">{cost.iap.products.map(p=><li><span>{p.name}</span><strong>{p.display_price}</strong></li>)}</ul><p class="lib-note">{cost.iap.storefront.toUpperCase()} App Store · {dateLabel(cost.iap.checked)}. Listed offers can differ from a personal checkout, country or web price.</p></>:<p>No verified in-app price list in the retrieved source.</p>}<p class="lib-review-state">Facts reviewed · transaction behaviour not yet assessed</p></div></div>:finding?<article class="lib-design-finding" id={'finding-'+d.id}><div class="lib-finding-layout">{evidence.at(-1)&&<figure><a href={evidence.at(-1).url}><img src={evidence.at(-1).image} width="1320" height="2868" alt={evidence.at(-1).screen_name} loading="lazy"/></a><figcaption><a href={evidence.at(-1).url}>Inspect the captured evidence</a></figcaption></figure>}<div class="lib-finding-reason"><p class="lib-finding-status">{names[finding.status]}</p><h4>{finding.scope}</h4><p>{finding.reason}</p><p class="lib-finding-limit">{finding.limits}</p><div class="lib-evidence-links">{evidence.map((s,n)=><a href={s.url}>Capture {n+1}</a>)}<a href={'#principle-'+d.principle_ids[0]}>Principle checklist</a></div></div></div></article>:d.id==='attention_agency'&&!review?<div><p>{attention.length?'Captured examples show '+attention.map(s=>s.screen_name).slice(0,3).join(', ')+'. Their presence alone does not establish pressure or coercion.':'Reminder defaults, cadence, streak loss and return-after-absence behaviour are not established by the published captures.'}</p><div class="lib-evidence-links">{attention.slice(0,3).map(s=><a href={s.url}>{s.screen_name}</a>)}</div><p class="lib-note">Next checks: opt-in, editable timing, pause, recovery and guilt/urgency wording. Delivered-message frequency awaits the notification study; a notification permission prompt is not a delivery log.</p></div>:review?<div class="lib-reviewed-dimension"><p>{review.review_summary}</p><h4>Checks still needed</h4><ul>{review.next_checks.map(c=><li>{c}</li>)}</ul><p class="lib-note">Evidence reviewed {dateLabel(review.reviewed)}. No ethical finding has been assigned from these facts alone.</p></div>:<p class="lib-muted">No scoped evaluation has been completed for this dimension. Screens and ingredients below can support further review; missing findings do not mean a pass, failure or absent feature.</p>}
 {review&&d.id==='money_access'&&<p class="lib-note">Evidence reviewed {dateLabel(review.reviewed)}. {review.next_checks.join(' ')}</p>}
 </section>;})}
 </div>
 <section class="lib-frame-key" id="redemptive-frame" data-pagefind-ignore="all"><h3>The redemptive frame</h3><p><strong>Exploitative:</strong> subverts agency. <strong>Ethical:</strong> respects people and safeguards. <strong>Redemptive:</strong> restores at a cost freely borne by the builder.</p><p class="lib-note">Specific practices, not an overall app grade. <a href="/apps/assessment/">Read the method and evidence requirements</a> · <a href="https://www.praxis.co/redemptive-entrepreneurship">Praxis’s frame</a>.</p></section>
 <details class="lib-principle-checklist" id="principle-checklist" data-pagefind-ignore="all"><summary>Full principle checklist <span>{findings.length} scoped finding{findings.length===1?'':'s'} · additional flow checks pending</span></summary><p class="lib-note">This is a map of the review, not a score. A linked finding informs a principle; it does not automatically grade that principle or the whole app. Unknown is not a pass or a failure.</p>{places.map(([place,title])=><section class="lib-principle-group"><h3>{title}</h3><dl>{rubric.principles.filter(p=>p.place===place).map(p=>{const linked=findings.filter(([,d])=>d.principle_ids.includes(p.id));return <div id={'principle-'+p.id}><dt><a href={p.url}>{p.name}</a><p>{p.question}</p></dt><dd>{linked.length?linked.map(([id,d])=><a href={'#finding-'+id}>Read the related scoped finding</a>):<span class="lib-muted">No scoped finding yet</span>}</dd></div>;})}</dl></section>)}<details class="lib-source-details"><summary>Coverage of the eight assessment dimensions</summary><dl class="lib-coverage-dimensions">{rubric.dimensions.map(d=>{const finding=findings.find(([id])=>id===d.id);return <div><dt>{d.label}</dt><dd>{finding?<a href={'#finding-'+d.id}>{names[finding[1].status]}</a>:a?.dimension_reviews?.[d.id]?<a href={'#dimension-'+d.id}>Reviewed; further evidence needed</a>:'Not assessed'}</dd></div>;})}</dl></details></details>

</section>
<ProfileSelector/>
